  "purpose": {
    "summary": "Maps coupling geometry between co-active regimes; identifies domain-locked and cross-domain regime dependencies.",
    "detail": "The RIM receives the raw structural frame registered by the Structural Faultline Detector and constructs a regime coupling graph — a directed graph in which nodes are active regimes and edges represent their mechanical dependencies (lock-in, veto, amplification, or suppression relationships). The RIM classifies each edge as domain-locked (both regimes in the same domain) or cross-domain (regimes spanning domain boundaries). Cross-domain interlock edges are reported to the CROSS_DOMAIN_CAUSALITY_WEAVER for inclusion in the CDCS."
  },
